{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>It is jubilee.</b> From the root of leading, as in ״יובילוה רגליה״, ״מי יובילני״, ״עיר מצור ביום ההוא יובל שי״." "<b>For you.</b> For Israel alone." "<b>It is jubilee, the fiftieth year.</b> What does this teach? Since it is stated ״וקדשתם את שנת החמישים שנה״, one might think that upon its entry it is sanctified from Rosh HaShanah, and upon its exit it continues on until Yom HaKippurim, for one does add from the profane to the holy. Therefore Scripture says: ״יובל היא שנת החמשים שנה תהיה לכם״ — its sanctification extends only until Rosh HaShanah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:12.735682366Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}